### Description

Search hosts under a specified resource scope with pagination, supporting filters by topology node, IPv4, IPv6, host name, OS name, and Agent status.

Resource scope supports business (`biz`), business set (`biz_set`), and tenant set (`tenant_set`): under a business, topology nodes can be used to narrow the range; a business set searches across all its sub-businesses; a tenant set searches across all hosts of the tenant (topology nodes do not take effect under business set / tenant set). IPv4, IPv6, host name, and OS name are all fuzzy matched (a match occurs when the value is similar to any keyword in the list); IPv6 supports compressed notation and is internally expanded to full form before matching. The caller must have access permission on the target resource scope.

### Request Parameters

#### Body Parameters

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| bk_scope_type | string | Yes | Resource scope type. Possible values: `biz` (business), `biz_set` (business set), `tenant_set` (tenant set) |
| bk_scope_id | string | Yes | Resource scope ID corresponding to `bk_scope_type`, representing a business ID, business-set ID, or tenant-set ID |
| topo_node_list | array | No | Topology node list used to narrow the search range. Three semantics (consistent across all resource scopes): (1) when omitted or `null`, topology nodes are not used as a filter and all hosts under the resource scope are returned; (2) when an empty array `[]` is passed, it is treated as "no matching node" (usually the empty result of an upstream intersection) and an empty list is returned directly (`total=0`, `data=[]`) without querying; (3) when a non-empty node list is passed, hosts are filtered by nodes. Node filtering only takes effect when `bk_scope_type` is `biz` (business); under business set / tenant set a non-empty node list is ignored (i.e. the whole resource scope is searched) |
| ipv4_key_list | array | No | IPv4 keyword list, fuzzy match; a host IPv4 matches when it is similar to any keyword in the list |
| ipv6_key_list | array | No | IPv6 keyword list, fuzzy match; compressed notation is supported; a host IPv6 matches when it is similar to any keyword in the list |
| host_name_key_list | array | No | Host name keyword list, fuzzy match; a host name matches when it is similar to any keyword in the list |
| os_name_key_list | array | No | OS name keyword list, fuzzy match; an OS name matches when it is similar to any keyword in the list |
| alive | int | No | Agent status filter. Possible values: `0` (abnormal), `1` (normal); not filtered by Agent status when omitted. This status is the Agent status persisted by the Job platform and may not be real-time |
| offset | int | No | Pagination offset starting from 0; defaults to 0 if omitted; must be greater than or equal to 0 |
| length | int | No | Number of records per page; defaults to 10 if omitted; valid range is 1 to 200 |

##### topo_node_list[] item

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| object_id | string | Yes | Node type ID. Possible values: `biz` (business), `set` (set), `module` (module) |
| instance_id | long | Yes | Node instance ID |

### Request Example

- POST

```json
{
  "bk_scope_type": "biz",
  "bk_scope_id": "2",
  "topo_node_list": [
    {
      "object_id": "module",
      "instance_id": 100
    }
  ],
  "ipv4_key_list": ["127.0.0.1"],
  "ipv6_key_list": ["::1"],
  "host_name_key_list": ["host"],
  "os_name_key_list": ["linux"],
  "alive": 1,
  "offset": 0,
  "length": 10
}
```

